title open problem 2: growth into material the other side divided

# Section 15, open problem 2.  One side adds a name to a pool the
# other side split.  The new name has to land in ONE of the fragments
# and nothing says which, so the current rule refuses.  Two shapes of
# arrival, one folder each.
#
# grow/ -- off-of hard-links a brand new name into the pool.  The new
#   name has no antecedent, so it arrives as an attachment and link L3
#   ties it to its pool; onto's split excludes the pool's names from
#   each other; L3 and the exclusion meet.
#
# move/ -- off-of moves an existing name in: stray.bin stops being its
#   own file and becomes another name for the pool's dnode.  This one
#   arrives with an antecedent, so it is a move link L2 rather than an
#   attachment, and it meets the same exclusion.
#
# Two refinements were tried and dropped: follow the fragment holding
# the most surviving names, and follow the dnode-continuing fragment.
# The first turns the answer on a count no user intended; the second
# turns it on which fragment the allocator happened to keep the old
# dnode for.  Change onto's dnode placement below (put 10-100 on b.bin
# instead of a.bin) and watch the second refinement change its mind
# while nothing about the user's intent changed.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: grow/
      10-100: a.bin = ab-v1
      10-100: b.bin
    3-100: move/
      20-100: p.bin = pq-v1
      20-100: q.bin
      21-100: stray.bin = pq-v1

tree onto
  1-1: /
    2-100: grow/
      # the split: two dnodes where there was one.
      10-100: a.bin = ab-v1
      210-200: b.bin = ab-v1
    3-100: move/
      # the same split, on the other pool.
      20-100: p.bin = pq-v1
      220-200: q.bin = pq-v1
      21-100: stray.bin = pq-v1

tree offof
  1-1: /
    2-100: grow/
      # a third link into the undivided pool.
      10-100: a.bin = ab-v1
      10-100: b.bin
      10-100: c.bin
    3-100: move/
      # stray.bin moves in: dnode 21 is gone and the name is now a
      # third name for dnode 20.
      20-100: p.bin = pq-v1
      20-100: q.bin
      20-100: stray.bin

# --- expected result, generated by gen-expected.js ---
expect conflict pooling
expect quarantined /grow/a.bin
expect quarantined /grow/b.bin
expect quarantined /move/p.bin
expect quarantined /move/q.bin
expect quarantined /move/stray.bin

tree expected
  1-1: /
    2-100: grow
      10-100: a.bin = ab-v1
      210-200: b.bin = ab-v1
    3-100: move
      20-100: p.bin = pq-v1
      220-200: q.bin = pq-v1
      21-100: stray.bin = pq-v1
